Turn completed.
1. Work performed: added the sequential cuBLASLt direct-MoE path in [expert_layer.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/expert_layer.cpp#L766) and dispatched it from the direct-MoE decode branch in [expert_layer.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/expert_layer.cpp#L1713). I also extended the packed-weight view to carry cuBLASLt scale pointers in [fused_moe_decode.h](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/include/nemotron/fused_moe_decode.h), generalized the NVFP4 GEMM runner to accept packed weight views in [nvfp4_gemm_runner.h](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/include/nemotron/nvfp4_gemm_runner.h#L39) and [nvfp4_gemm_runner.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/nvfp4_gemm_runner.cpp#L176), and added small device ops for `relu2` and scaled accumulation in [primitive_ops.cu](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/primitive_ops.cu#L26).

2. How the cuBLASLt path is structured: it keeps the existing host-side `SelectTopExperts` routing, packs the normalized single-token row to NVFP4 once, then runs routed experts sequentially as `up_proj GEMM -> relu2 -> repack -> down_proj GEMM -> scale/accumulate`, then runs the shared expert with the same `up/down` pattern, and finishes with `routed + shared + residual` on device in [expert_layer.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/expert_layer.cpp#L806) and [expert_layer.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/expert_layer.cpp#L1719). I also moved the latent-path scratch allocations out of the direct-MoE fastpath so it no longer allocates those tensors before the direct return path.

3. How `matmul_block_scales` are handled: `MonolithicNvfp4ExpertWeights` now allocates a parallel swizzled `matmul_block_scales` buffer and writes it at `UploadExpert()` time via `SwizzleRowMajorNvfp4ScalesForExecution`, while tensor scales are stored with a 16-byte stride so expert-local pointers remain cuBLASLt-plan-safe in [monolithic_expert_weights.cu](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/monolithic_expert_weights.cu#L47) and [monolithic_expert_weights.cu](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/monolithic_expert_weights.cu#L169). `GetView()` now returns both raw block scales for the old fused kernel and swizzled scales for the new cuBLASLt path in [monolithic_expert_weights.cu](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/monolithic_expert_weights.cu#L224).

4. Compile status: `cmake --build build-phase1-tests --target nemotron_runtime_backend -j4` passed. `cmake --build build-phase1-tests --target full_forward_manifest_smoke_test` also passed; the first attempt failed only because I accidentally launched both target builds concurrently and they raced on `libnemotron_runtime_backend.a`, so I reran the second build sequentially and it completed cleanly. I also recorded the checkpoint in [PLAN.md](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/proj-2026-04-01-1534/PLAN.md#L181).

5. Concerns about correctness: this turn only verified compilation, not runtime correctness or throughput. The new path still inherits the current per-op synchronizations inside NVFP4 packing, GEMM execution, and the new primitive ops, so it should remove the scalar fused kernel bottleneck but still needs the actual smoke/correctness run and a fresh profile to confirm the expected drop in MoE time.

CHECKPOINT: 6
